Yugara have walked for a thousand years.

519
00:34:21,820 --> 00:34:25,460
Where exactly are you,
Karoo, trying to go?

520
00:34:33,640 --> 00:34:34,470
What's that?

521
00:34:35,060 --> 00:34:37,440
You'd like to stay here on Zo? Yes.

522
00:34:37,900 --> 00:34:39,620
And what do you mean to do?

523
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:42,760
To be honest, I don't know for certain.

524
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:45,130
However...

525
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:49,150
Understood.

526
00:34:51,060 --> 00:34:54,680
If possible, I intend to
have another conversation.

527
00:34:56,140 --> 00:34:57,280
With Zunisha.

528
00:34:59,340 --> 00:35:01,560
The one who's lived a thousand years.

529
00:35:04,420 --> 00:35:07,538
I wish to know why this
creature could hear my voice.

530
00:35:09,520 --> 00:35:14,157
I need to see if Zunisha knows
anything about the Kozuki clan.

531
00:35:14,240 --> 00:35:15,580
What's all this?

532
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:17,760
Do my ears deceive me?

533
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:20,160
Yes, I see.

534
00:35:20,520 --> 00:35:23,638
But what about the ones who
await our return to Wano?

535
00:35:25,160 --> 00:35:26,460
Don't fret, Kitomon.

536
00:35:27,740 --> 00:35:30,564
Kaido is still a serious
threat to this country,

537
00:35:30,700 --> 00:35:33,229
so protecting Zo weighs
heavily on my mind.

538
00:35:33,680 --> 00:35:38,209
And Jack was somehow able to navigate
here and attack us not once, but twice.

539
00:35:38,340 --> 00:35:41,046
It would be foolish to
let our guard down now.

540
00:35:43,400 --> 00:35:47,400
A large group like this can't simply
roll into Wano all at one time.

541
00:35:48,840 --> 00:35:53,300
I think it's best if I remain here
for a while, but when I do depart,

542
00:35:53,720 --> 00:35:54,896
please come with me.

543
00:35:56,860 --> 00:35:59,397
Earlier, Cat Viper created
a Vever card for me.

544
00:35:59,480 --> 00:36:00,940
Please distribute this.

545
00:36:01,340 --> 00:36:05,020
I propose that we
separate into four teams.

546
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:11,280
Our mission is to overthrow Kaido, as well
as the Shogun who rules the land of Wado.

547
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:15,617
You can navigate there by
way of the beaver card.

548
00:36:15,700 --> 00:36:17,582
The only issue is correspondence

549
00:36:19,200 --> 00:36:20,577
in other countries.

550
00:36:20,660 --> 00:36:22,537
There's a strange mollusks.

551
00:36:22,620 --> 00:36:24,937
How to explain it?

552
00:36:25,020 --> 00:36:27,097
It facilitates communication.

553
00:36:27,180 --> 00:36:29,417
They're called transponder snails.

554
00:36:29,500 --> 00:36:30,377
Oh of course,

555
00:36:30,460 --> 00:36:34,537
I'm familiar with them but sadly we
don't have that custom in our country.

556
00:36:34,620 --> 00:36:38,440
Actually, I noticed a wild
one back in the forest.

557
00:36:40,120 --> 00:36:44,020
If you can go snag one, I'll
set it up for you. It's easy.

558
00:36:44,220 --> 00:36:46,040
I had no idea.

559
00:36:47,440 --> 00:36:48,270
Hey!

560
00:36:49,340 --> 00:36:50,170
Hey!

561
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:55,580
Lion Viper's house fell apart!

562
00:36:56,500 --> 00:36:57,540
I'm here!

563
00:36:57,700 --> 00:36:58,800
Help me find you!

564
00:36:59,080 --> 00:37:00,140
Are you okay?

565
00:37:00,560 --> 00:37:01,640
Answer me!

566
00:37:02,100 --> 00:37:04,300
Lion Viper! Hello?

567
00:37:04,820 --> 00:37:06,020
I'm over here!

568
00:37:06,400 --> 00:37:07,230
Over where?

569
00:37:07,313 --> 00:37:09,520
Just look down!

570
00:37:12,040 --> 00:37:13,180
It's the turtle!

571
00:37:14,180 --> 00:37:15,580
Give me some room!

572
00:37:20,180 --> 00:37:23,500
Gonna fell over cover in peace? Get out!

573
00:37:24,180 --> 00:37:25,040
It's you!

574
00:37:25,260 --> 00:37:27,260
Guess you're the turtle viper now!

575
00:37:27,600 --> 00:37:29,797
Well, kid, you always get my name wrong,

576
00:37:29,880 --> 00:37:32,837
but taking out the lion part
somehow makes it even worse.

577
00:37:32,920 --> 00:37:33,750
Quit it!

578
00:37:33,833 --> 00:37:35,160
How did you survive that?

579
00:37:35,360 --> 00:37:36,937
The whole building got destroyed!

580
00:37:37,020 --> 00:37:41,817
Of course I survived, because I'm the man
with the power of the Turtle Turtle Fruit.

581
00:37:41,900 --> 00:37:42,920
You saw my shell.

582
00:37:43,060 --> 00:37:45,119
It's hard and durable like diamond.

583
00:37:45,220 --> 00:37:46,480
Are you listening?

584
00:37:47,220 --> 00:37:50,197
Jeffers said he would be in charge
of making sure you get better,

585
00:37:50,280 --> 00:37:51,397
so you don't have to worry.

586
00:37:51,480 --> 00:37:52,421
You little brat.

587
00:37:52,540 --> 00:37:56,117
I was kind of expecting a big reaction
to that part about the diamond.

588
00:37:56,200 --> 00:37:57,030
Get out.

589
00:37:58,140 --> 00:38:00,300
I do appreciate his help, though.

590
00:38:02,020 --> 00:38:04,100
I owe an awful lot to you guys.

591
00:38:10,380 --> 00:38:11,840
No time to chat!

592
00:38:12,140 --> 00:38:13,840
To Big Mom's house we go!

593
00:38:16,220 --> 00:38:17,920
Slow down, dammit!

594
00:38:18,140 --> 00:38:21,846
I'm at the brink of death over
here, so take it easy, would ya?

595
00:38:26,060 --> 00:38:26,980
Listen, you!

596
00:38:27,200 --> 00:38:29,540
I'm still recovering! Watch it!

597
00:38:31,880 --> 00:38:33,240
This isn't fair!

598
00:38:33,480 --> 00:38:35,000
I don't believe it!

599
00:38:35,220 --> 00:38:36,217
Why is it you?

600
00:38:36,300 --> 00:38:39,180
Of all the guys I gotta hold my life to!

601
00:38:44,520 --> 00:38:45,350
Master.

602
00:38:46,360 --> 00:38:47,340
Yes, Pedro?

603
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:49,784
Sanji saved our entire country.

604
00:38:53,240 --> 00:38:56,000
And he was abducted
right here on our soil.

605
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:59,700
I know we can't take many,
but I have one request.

606
00:39:00,360 --> 00:39:05,184
Peccombs mustn't be the only member of the
Mink tribe to accompany the Straw Hats.

607
00:39:06,020 --> 00:39:07,077
I take it.

608
00:39:07,160 --> 00:39:10,740
You, Karoo, would like to join
Luffy on his trip? Yes, sir.

609
00:39:11,300 --> 00:39:12,860
Not so fast there, Pedro!

610
00:39:13,780 --> 00:39:15,720
You dare upstage us?

611
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:24,260
This task is better suited to my
group, the Dark Storm Musketeers!

612
00:39:25,200 --> 00:39:26,557
Forget it, Shishilian.

613
00:39:26,640 --> 00:39:29,052
This is supposed to be a stealth mission.

614
00:39:29,140 --> 00:39:31,560
And you're an insufferable loudmouth!

615
00:39:33,020 --> 00:39:34,960
Where did that come from?

616
00:39:36,160 --> 00:39:38,000
Please, sir, I should go along.

617
00:39:38,340 --> 00:39:40,637
I've been with the Straw
Hats since they got here.

618
00:39:40,720 --> 00:39:41,550
And me.

619
00:39:41,633 --> 00:39:42,680
Send me as Dr.

620
00:39:42,780 --> 00:39:43,917
Chopper's assistant.

621
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:46,160
Hold on a minute. But wait!

622
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:48,277
We became good friends with Luffy.

623
00:39:48,360 --> 00:39:49,560
Let us go!

624
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:51,700
After attacking him...

625
00:39:52,540 --> 00:39:53,560
I should go.

626
00:39:53,780 --> 00:39:55,677
Nami likes sleeping on my stomach.

627
00:39:55,760 --> 00:39:58,231
What's that got to do with anything, Yomo?

628
00:39:58,420 --> 00:40:03,960
Choose me so I can nibble on Baron Corpse's
bones whenever I want. And me. And me.

629
00:40:04,320 --> 00:40:05,880
That's just plain selfish.

630
00:40:06,380 --> 00:40:07,697
You guys aren't coming.

631
00:40:07,780 --> 00:40:10,200
I know exactly how you gotta feel.

632
00:40:10,460 --> 00:40:14,280
But the wisest thing to
do is to let Pedro go.

633
00:40:18,480 --> 00:40:20,760
But why? Him, master! Hmm?

634
00:40:22,940 --> 00:40:24,820
Because Peckoms will be going.

635
00:40:28,420 --> 00:40:30,780
Only Pedro can keep him in check.

636
00:40:31,280 --> 00:40:32,940
I see no other option.

637
00:40:39,200 --> 00:40:41,400
What is all this excitement about?

638
00:40:43,500 --> 00:40:47,357
I know we used the word perfect to
describe one of the previous models,

639
00:40:47,440 --> 00:40:50,680
but my latest creation blows
them all out of the water.

640
00:40:51,640 --> 00:40:52,620
Check it out.

641
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:55,517
I incorporated the growth
capability of Pop Green,

642
00:40:55,600 --> 00:40:59,557
and Franky lent me some of his
expertise for the surface treatment.

643
00:40:59,640 --> 00:41:02,737
I don't want to say it's the
greatest invention of the century,

644
00:41:02,820 --> 00:41:04,349
but that wouldn't be wrong

645
00:41:05,880 --> 00:41:07,460
Are you listening, Nami?

646
00:41:07,720 --> 00:41:09,544
What happens when I squeeze it?

647
00:41:19,700 --> 00:41:20,800
That was close

648
00:41:28,700 --> 00:41:29,800
I can't use this.

649
00:41:29,940 --> 00:41:30,997
You made it wait too long.

650
00:41:31,080 --> 00:41:32,917
That's an improved climate
attack that can change

651
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:35,517
its length when you apply
a tiny amount of pressure.

652
00:41:35,600 --> 00:41:37,129
It's a feature, not a bug.

653
00:41:39,520 --> 00:41:40,860
Right, I get it now.

654
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:44,117
I mixed in different elements from all the

655
00:41:44,200 --> 00:41:46,847
Witheria gadgets I got
from you and Zeff Odi.

656
00:41:49,660 --> 00:41:51,484
There's just one thing, though.

657
00:41:53,420 --> 00:41:57,008
Remember what you said to me
about your other climate attack?

658
00:42:01,480 --> 00:42:03,700
It's just like having a magic wand.

659
00:42:04,100 --> 00:42:06,500
I didn't understand what you meant then.

660
00:42:06,900 --> 00:42:08,080
This is so easy.

661
00:42:08,260 --> 00:42:09,495
It's the perfect fit.

662
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:11,220
I'll stop talking now.

663
00:42:11,380 --> 00:42:12,720
I love this thing.

664
00:42:13,320 --> 00:42:14,150
Some skill.

665
00:42:14,440 --> 00:42:16,675
That must be highly advanced in jutsu.

666
00:42:17,320 --> 00:42:18,660
It's so awesome.

667
00:42:19,040 --> 00:42:22,537
It's like you took all the science
of Witheria to the absolute limit.

668
00:42:22,620 --> 00:42:25,757
This is the sorcery climate
act I've always dreamed about.

669
00:42:25,840 --> 00:42:26,670
Thanks, Usopp.

670
00:42:26,753 --> 00:42:27,583
You're the best.

671
00:42:27,666 --> 00:42:28,700
No trouble at all.

672
00:42:28,980 --> 00:42:30,180
Glad you like it.

673
00:42:30,340 --> 00:42:32,977
Now, the materials weren't free, so...

674
00:42:33,060 --> 00:42:36,120
Let's try a mirage tempo. You cheapskate!

675
00:42:40,920 --> 00:42:42,360
Guess this is everybody.

676
00:42:44,440 --> 00:42:46,140
So, Pierre, you ready?

677
00:42:46,360 --> 00:42:48,125
It's Pedro, but yes, let's go.

678
00:42:48,400 --> 00:42:52,700
Uh, hey, nobody told me
he was coming. Get out!

679
00:42:52,980 --> 00:42:56,657
I thought I'd better tag along, since I've
known you, Karoo, for such a long time.

680
00:42:56,740 --> 00:42:59,140
What's that supposed to mean? Get off!

681
00:43:00,060 --> 00:43:00,890
Kashi!

682
00:43:01,280 --> 00:43:03,380
Nami, please be careful.

683
00:43:04,180 --> 00:43:05,480
I'll do my best.

684
00:43:05,680 --> 00:43:06,621
Take care, okay?

685
00:43:09,400 --> 00:43:10,400
Goodbye, Doctor.

686
00:43:10,800 --> 00:43:11,740
Best of luck.

687
00:43:18,680 --> 00:43:19,680
Here's the thing.

688
00:43:19,800 --> 00:43:22,977
It's him we're talking about, so
he might be happy about all this.

689
00:43:23,060 --> 00:43:25,917
I mean, maybe that idiot skirt
chaser does want to get married.

690
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:26,960
That's crazy!

691
00:43:27,320 --> 00:43:29,140
But I guess you're not wrong.

692
00:43:29,640 --> 00:43:31,760
Ah, I'm sure it'll be fine.

693
00:43:32,420 --> 00:43:34,200
Sir Luffy, fare thee well.

694
00:43:34,400 --> 00:43:36,597
We shall wait for you in the Land of Wano.

695
00:43:36,680 --> 00:43:38,020
Do your best, Luffy!

696
00:43:39,660 --> 00:43:41,280
Go out of trouble, okay?

697
00:43:42,920 --> 00:43:45,685
Be sure to let us know
if anything bad happens.

698
00:43:45,780 --> 00:43:49,015
I'll make some bad-ass weapons
so we can go whoop-kado!

699
00:43:49,300 --> 00:43:52,617
And I'll round up every last samurai
the Land of Wano has to offer.

700
00:43:52,700 --> 00:43:53,530
Huh?

701
00:43:53,980 --> 00:43:54,810
Know this.

702
00:43:55,120 --> 00:43:57,473
Allow me to assist you with the descent.

703
00:43:57,580 --> 00:43:59,340
Nah, that's okay. We got it.

704
00:44:07,240 --> 00:44:08,070
Bye.

705
00:44:10,640 --> 00:44:11,470
Yahoo!

706
00:44:30,440 --> 00:44:33,180
We'll get Sanji back before you know him.

707
00:44:35,260 --> 00:44:38,460
See you guys when we get to Wado. Right.

708
00:44:38,660 --> 00:44:40,200
Be careful around Big Mom.

709
00:44:40,560 --> 00:44:42,854
There's a good reason she's an emperor.

710
00:44:43,280 --> 00:44:44,110
OK.

711
00:44:52,700 --> 00:44:54,465
With Luffy leading the charge,

712
00:44:54,720 --> 00:44:57,737
the Sanji Retrieval Team sets
out for Whole Cake Island,

713
00:44:57,820 --> 00:45:02,340
where Luffy will face off against
formidable former adversary, Big Mom.

714
00:45:03,620 --> 00:45:08,900
Meanwhile, on the Grand Line, in the
Kingdom of San called Alabasta...

715
00:45:10,260 --> 00:45:11,340
Hurry up, Father!

716
00:45:11,520 --> 00:45:12,397
Slow down, Vivi.

717
00:45:12,480 --> 00:45:14,362
Why are you in such a good mood?

718
00:45:26,080 --> 00:45:26,910
Why not?

719
00:45:27,120 --> 00:45:29,826
It's been a long time
since I went out to sea.
